#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# divisor_sum

#% text
# `divisor_sum(n, f)` gives the sum of `f(d)` over the positive divisors `d` of `n`.

#% text
# `divisor_sum(n, f, cond)` sums only over the divisors `d` with `cond(d)` true.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `f` and `cond` are functions of one argument, such as `d => d^2` or a named function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
divisor_sum(12, d => d)
#% output
#= 28

#% cell
divisor_sum(12, d => 1)
#% output
#= 6

#% cell
divisor_sum(30, d => d^2)
#% output
#= 1300

#% cell
divisor_sum(36, d => d, d => is_odd(d))
#% output
#= 13

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Moebius inversion: the sum of `moebius_mu(d)` is 0 for `n > 1`:

#% cell
divisor_sum(60, moebius_mu)
#% output
#= 0

#% text
# Gauss's identity, the totients of the divisors add up to `n`:

#% cell
divisor_sum(100, euler_phi)
#% output
#= 100

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `divisors`, `divisor_sigma`, `moebius_mu`, `euler_phi`
